---
name: quick-fix-pr
description: Small, well-specified changes — implement from the ticket (no plan step), verify, lint, open a PR, and run one review with at most one re-review
version: "1.0.0"
target_types:
  - worktree
hints:
  - The implement agent's brief is the ticket itself. Have it fetch the full ticket and its comments, and ask for feedback instead of guessing when the ticket lacks clear acceptance criteria
  - Use this for small changes only (a few files, clear acceptance criteria, prompt and workflow edits, small bugs). Keep ticket-to-pr for anything that needs a plan
  - The single re-review is deliberate. If the repo wants more cycles, call iterate-pr instead of inlining the review
  - "The review-scope script picks each review's scope: \"incremental\" from the commit the last <!-- conductor-review --> review was submitted on (exported as review_since) when that commit is still an ancestor of HEAD, otherwise \"full\". Never hard-code incremental: the first review must cover the whole PR. Optional customization (not in this template body): when HEAD is already the commit the last conductor review was submitted on, skip the re-review. To add it, give the workflow a force_review input (default \"false\") passed to review-scope as FORCE_REVIEW, then guard the review-pr call with unless review-scope.reuse_review and add, under if review-scope.reuse_review, a script step named review-aggregator (reuse-review.sh) hands triage that review's verdict and findings, read from a base64 payload submit-review embeds in the review body (only from a non-dismissed review by an OWNER/MEMBER/COLLABORATOR or by a bot named in TRUSTED_REVIEW_BOTS, otherwise review-scope falls back to a full review; pass TRUSTED_REVIEW_BOTS to both review-scope and reuse-review, set to the repo's reviewer GitHub App login such as conductor-ai-reviewer[bot], because GitHub reports app reviewers as author_association NONE; copy lib-trusted-review.sh with the scripts, which source it). The review-scope script emits reuse_review, and force_review = true restores the full re-review"
  - Check the repo's CI config (.github/workflows/ or similar) and customize the verify, fmt-fix and lint-fix commands to match it
  - "verify is a script, not an agent: exit codes decide pass or fail. Write .conductor/scripts/verify.sh to run the repo's build, test, lint and format checks on what changed since the merge base with FEATURE_BASE_BRANCH, skip them when nothing relevant changed, and emit a FLOW_OUTPUT with the has_failures marker on any failure and a context naming the failing checks, test names and first error lines (implement reads it). A check that can't run is a failure. After the tests pass, rerun just the tests the diff adds or changes a few more times (bounded by a count limit and a time cap) and fail as flaky on any failure, so a timing-dependent new test fails verify instead of CI"
---
workflow quick-fix-pr {
  meta {
    description = "Small, well-specified changes: implement from the ticket, verify, lint, open a PR, and run one review with at most one re-review"
    trigger     = "manual"
    targets     = ["worktree"]
    group       = "Development"
  }

  inputs {
    ticket_id required
  }

  call implement-ticket {
    retries = 2
    as      = "developer"
  }

  script verify {
    run = ".conductor/scripts/verify.sh"
    env = { FEATURE_BASE_BRANCH = "{{feature_base_branch}}" }
  }

  call workflow lint-fix

  script fmt-fix {
    run = ".conductor/scripts/fmt-fix.sh"
  }

  script push-and-pr {
    run = ".conductor/scripts/push-and-pr.sh"
    as  = "developer"
    env = { FEATURE_BASE_BRANCH = "{{feature_base_branch}}" }
  }

  unless push-and-pr.no_changes {
    script review-scope {
      run = ".conductor/scripts/review-scope.sh"
      env = { PR_NUMBER = "{{pr_number}}" }
    }

    call workflow review-pr {
      inputs {
        scope = "{{review_scope}}"
        since = "{{review_since}}"
      }
    }

    if review-pr.has_blocking_findings {
      call address-reviews {
        as = "developer"
      }

      script fmt-fix-review {
        run = ".conductor/scripts/fmt-fix.sh"
      }

      script push {
        run = ".conductor/scripts/push.sh"
        as  = "developer"
      }

      script review-scope-rereview {
        run = ".conductor/scripts/review-scope.sh"
        env = { PR_NUMBER = "{{pr_number}}" }
      }

      call workflow review-pr {
        inputs {
          scope = "{{review_scope}}"
          since = "{{review_since}}"
        }
      }

      if review-pr.has_blocking_findings {
        gate human_review {
          prompt     = "quick-fix-pr allows one re-review, and it still requests changes. Address the findings by hand, or rerun as ticket-to-pr or iterate-pr."
          timeout    = "72h"
          on_timeout = fail
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
